<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" style="margin:0;padding:0;">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>You're one of our first 300 users</title>
    <style>
      @media (max-width: 640px) {
        .email-container {
          width: 100% !important;
          margin: 0 !important;
          border-radius: 0 !important;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body
    style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#f5f7fb;font-family:'Segoe UI',Arial,sans-serif;color:#0f172a;"
  >
    <table
      role="presentation"
      cellpadding="0"
      cellspacing="0"
      width="100%"
      style="background:#f5f7fb;padding:32px 0;"
    >
      <tr>
        <td align="center">
          <table
            role="presentation"
            class="email-container"
            cellpadding="0"
            cellspacing="0"
            width="640"
            style="width:640px;max-width:640px;background:#ffffff;border-radius:16px;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;overflow:hidden;"
          >
            <tr>
              <td
                style="padding:28px 20px;text-align:center;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb;"
              >
                <div
                  style="font-size:26px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#111827;"
                >
                  KickerGPT
                </div>
                <div
                  style="margin-top:6px;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.28em;color:#6b7280;text-transform:uppercase;"
                >
                  Football intelligence
                </div>
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td style="padding:28px 32px 10px;line-height:1.6;font-size:15px;">
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">Hey {{name}},</p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
                  You're among the first 300 people using KickerGPT, and I wanted
                  to reach out personally.
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Here's the problem we're solving:</strong></p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
                  Everyone knows Man City should beat Ipswich. But sometimes they
                  don't. And when that happens, it's not because you picked
                  wrong—it's because there were factors you couldn't see.
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
                  Maybe City played 3 matches in 8 days. Maybe the referee has a
                  pattern with big teams. Maybe Ipswich performs completely
                  differently on Saturdays. Maybe the weather mirrors a past
                  upset.
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
                  These patterns exist in the data. Most people just don't look.
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>That's what KickerGPT does.</strong></p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 8px;">We analyze 14 dimensions per match:</p>
                <ul style="margin:0 0 12px 18px;padding:0;color:#111827;">
                  <li style="margin:6px 0;">Head-to-head patterns</li>
                  <li style="margin:6px 0;">Day-of-week performance</li>
                  <li style="margin:6px 0;">Weather impact</li>
                  <li style="margin:6px 0;">Referee history with each team</li>
                  <li style="margin:6px 0;">Injury impact vs squad depth</li>
                  <li style="margin:6px 0;">Rest days and fatigue</li>
                  <li style="margin:6px 0;">Home/away splits</li>
                  <li style="margin:6px 0;">Momentum and streaks</li>
                  <li style="margin:6px 0;">Goal patterns (clean sheets, BTTS)</li>
                  <li style="margin:6px 0;">Upset history when teams are underdogs</li>
                  <li style="margin:6px 0;">And more...</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
                  It's not about predicting scores. It's about surfacing the insights
                  you'd never think to look for.
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>We need your help.</strong></p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
                  We're still early and want to make KickerGPT genuinely useful for
                  you. Would you take 2 minutes to share your feedback?
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 16px;text-align:center;">
                  <a
                    href="{{surveyLink}}"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener"
                    style="display:inline-block;padding:14px 28px;background:#111827;color:#ffffff;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;border-radius:10px;letter-spacing:0.02em;"
                  >
                    Share feedback
                  </a>
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;color:#4b5563;font-size:13px;text-align:center;">
                  If the button doesn't open, copy this link:
                  <br />
                  <span style="word-break:break-all;color:#1f2937;">{{surveyLink}}</span>
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>And here's a thank you:</strong></p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">
                  As one of our first 300, you get 90% off Pro (100 prompts/month instead of 10).
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 18px;">
                  <span
                    style="display:inline-block;padding:10px 14px;background:#eef2ff;border-radius:6px;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-weight:700;color:#312e81;"
                  >
                    {{promoCode}}
                  </span>
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;">Thanks for being here from the start.</p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 8px;">KickerGPT Team</p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 12px;color:#4b5563;">
                  P.S. — If KickerGPT has helped you spot something you wouldn't have seen
                  otherwise, I'd love to hear about it. Just reply to this email.
                </p>
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td
                style="padding:18px 28px;border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb;text-align:center;color:#6b7280;font-size:12px;"
              >
                If the button doesn’t work, copy this link into your browser:
                <br />
                <span style="word-break:break-all;color:#4b5563;">{{surveyLink}}</span>
                <br /><br />
                <a
                  href="{{unsubscribeUrl}}"
                  style="color:#4b5563;text-decoration:underline;"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener"
                >
                  Unsubscribe
                </a>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </table>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </body>
</html>
